# The list holds unboxed doubles, and it is as long as the counter says: a push stores at the counter. Whether there is room is asked once, in front of the loop, for all its turns.
# CHECK-LABEL: steps by 1
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[k]] = Phi(
# CHECK-NOT: Phi(
# CHECK-NOT: Below(
# CHECK: Double b@[[element]] = IToD(b@[[k]],
# CHECK: Store(b@[[element]], b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Writes:indexedDoubleProperties,
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[next]] = Add(b@[[k]], $1(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[goesOn]] = GreaterThan(b@{{*}}, b@[[next]], {{*}}:Less)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[goesOn]], Terminal, {{*}}:Less)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# NONE-LABEL: steps by 1
# NONE-NOT: Reads:JSObject_butterfly
# Nothing in the loop asks for the capacity or the length. The storage gets the length where the loop is left.
# NONE-NOT: Butterfly_vectorLength
# NONE-NOT: Butterfly_publicLength
# NONE-NOT: Reads:JSCell
# NONE-NOT: :CallDirect
# The turns can be counted ahead of the loop: where they are few it goes without its poll, and a copy of it that polls takes the others.
# NONE-NOT: Patchpoint(
# NONE-LABEL: end of loop
# The list is made with room for all the elements, since the loop says how many there will be, however many: where the stub makes no such list an operation reserves the room.
# CALLS: f1: size=
# CALLS: operation operationAOTReserveWholeArrayCapacity x1
# CALLS-NEXT: stub ArrayPush x1
# CALLS-NEXT: stub NewArrayWithLength.Double x1
# CALLS-NEXT: stub NewEmptyArray.DoubleDefaultCapacity x1
# CALLS-NOT: stub
# CALLS-NOT: operation
# CALLS: f{{*}}: size=
# Convert (two), store, count, test. From eight turns on, eight at a time.
# X64-NOT: , instructions:
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 5, patchpoints: 0
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 35, patchpoints: 0, rare instructions: 14
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 12, patchpoints: 1, rare instructions: 9, {{*}}entered rarely
# X64-NOT: , instructions:
# ARM64-NOT: , instructions:
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 4, patchpoints: 0
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 27, patchpoints: 0
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 13, patchpoints: 1, rare instructions: 4, {{*}}entered rarely
# ARM64-NOT: , instructions:
# In front of the loop: is there room for as many elements as the bound says?
# WAYS: Int32 b@[[capacity]] = Load(b@[[storage]], offset = -4, ControlDependent|Reads:Butterfly_vectorLength,
# WAYS: = {{*}}(b@{{*}}, b@{{*}}, {{*}}:AppendElement)
# The length is stored where the loop ends.
# WAYS: Store(b@{{*}}, b@[[storage]], offset = -8, ControlDependent|Writes:Butterfly_publicLength,
